IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `s121-nouns`
IMPORT `s121-support`
IMPORT `s121-a-exclusion`

-- 26 U.S.C. section 121. LAYER 1, module 6: subsection (b), the limitations.
-- The $250,000, $500,000, 2-year, 10-year and 2-year-absence figures and the date January 1, 2009 are the text's own.
-- "The gain" is a fact the caller states: what the gain is, is not defined by the section.
-- Nothing is rounded: the text does not say how, so the ratio of (b)(5)(B) is exact (fork F9).

§ `Subsection (b)(1): in general`

-- src:16 | (1) In general
-- src:17 | The amount of gain excluded from gross income under subsection (a) with respect to any sale or exchange shall not exceed $250,000.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(b)(1) (src:16-17)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 121(b)(1) the dollar limitation` MEANS 250_000

-- src:17 | The amount of gain excluded from gross income under subsection (a) with respect to any sale or exchange shall not exceed $250,000.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(b)(1) (src:17)
GIVEN gain IS A NUMBER
      limitation IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 121(b)(1) the amount of gain excluded, which shall not exceed the limitation` MEANS
    `the smaller of` gain limitation

§ `Subsection (b)(2): special rules for joint returns`

-- src:22 | (i) either spouse meets the ownership requirements of subsection (a) with respect to such property;
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(b)(2)(A)(i) (src:22)
GIVEN `the first spouse meets the ownership requirements` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the second spouse meets the ownership requirements` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(b)(2)(A)(i) either spouse meets the ownership requirements of subsection (a)` MEANS
    `either is true` `the first spouse meets the ownership requirements` `the second spouse meets the ownership requirements`

-- src:23 | (ii) both spouses meet the use requirements of subsection (a) with respect to such property; and
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(b)(2)(A)(ii) (src:23)
GIVEN `the first spouse meets the use requirements` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the second spouse meets the use requirements` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(b)(2)(A)(ii) both spouses meet the use requirements of subsection (a)` MEANS
    `both are true` `the first spouse meets the use requirements` `the second spouse meets the use requirements`

-- The bar of paragraph (3), as it applies to each spouse (JUST TRUE = the bar applies to that spouse).
-- src:24 | (iii) neither spouse is ineligible for the benefits of subsection (a) with respect to such property by reason of paragraph (3).
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(b)(2)(A)(iii) (src:24)
GIVEN `paragraph (3) bars the first spouse` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (3) bars the second spouse` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(b)(2)(A)(iii) neither spouse is ineligible by reason of paragraph (3)` MEANS
    `both are true` (`the opposite of` `paragraph (3) bars the first spouse`) (`the opposite of` `paragraph (3) bars the second spouse`)

-- src:18 | (2) Special rules for joint returns
-- src:19 | In the case of a husband and wife who make a joint return for the taxable year of the sale or exchange of the property—
-- src:20 | (A) $500,000 Limitation for certain joint returns
-- src:21 | Paragraph (1) shall be applied by substituting “$500,000” for “$250,000” if—
-- src:22 | (i) either spouse meets the ownership requirements of subsection (a) with respect to such property;
-- src:23 | (ii) both spouses meet the use requirements of subsection (a) with respect to such property; and
-- src:24 | (iii) neither spouse is ineligible for the benefits of subsection (a) with respect to such property by reason of paragraph (3).
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(b)(2)(A) (src:18-24)
GIVEN `a husband and wife make a joint return for the taxable year of the sale or exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
      `limb (i)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `limb (ii)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `limb (iii)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(b)(2)(A) paragraph (1) is applied by substituting $500,000 for $250,000` MEANS
    IF `a husband and wife make a joint return for the taxable year of the sale or exchange`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (1) shall be applied by substituting “$500,000” for “$250,000” if— (i) ...; (ii) ...; and (iii) ..." (a failed "if"; marginal reading (a) in NOTES.md)
    THEN `both are true` `limb (i)` (`both are true` `limb (ii)` `limb (iii)`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a husband and wife who make a joint return for the taxable year of the sale or exchange of the property" -- not a joint return is outside the paragraph's scope.
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:21 | Paragraph (1) shall be applied by substituting “$500,000” for “$250,000” if—
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(b)(2)(A) (src:21)
GIVEN `paragraph (2)(A) is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 121(b)(2)(A) the limitation under paragraph (1) as substituted` MEANS
    CONSIDER `paragraph (2)(A) is met`
    WHEN JUST yes THEN
        IF yes
        THEN JUST 500_000
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the substitution is made "if" the limbs are met; when they are not, this subparagraph substitutes nothing.
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- src:26 | If such spouses do not meet the requirements of subparagraph (A), the limitation under paragraph (1) shall be the sum of the limitations under paragraph (1) to which each spouse would be entitled if such spouses had not been married. For purposes of the preceding sentence, each spouse shall be treated as owning the property during the period that either spouse owned the property.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(b)(2)(B), the limitation to which a spouse would be entitled (src:26)
GIVEN `the spouse meets the ownership requirements, each spouse being treated as owning the property during the period that either spouse owned it` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the spouse meets the use requirements` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (3) bars the spouse` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 121(b)(2)(B) the limitation under paragraph (1) to which the spouse would be entitled if the spouses had not been married` MEANS
    IF entitled EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 121(b)(1) the dollar limitation`)
    ELSE IF entitled EQUALS NOTHING
         THEN NOTHING
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the limitation under paragraph (1) to which each spouse would be entitled if such spouses had not been married" -- a spouse who would not be entitled to subsection (a)'s benefits has no limitation to be entitled to (an entitlement, not a power: marginal reading (a) and fork F13)
         ELSE JUST 0
    WHERE
        entitled MEANS `both are true` (`both are true` `the spouse meets the ownership requirements, each spouse being treated as owning the property during the period that either spouse owned it` `the spouse meets the use requirements`) (`the opposite of` `paragraph (3) bars the spouse`)

-- src:25 | (B) Other joint returns
-- src:26 | If such spouses do not meet the requirements of subparagraph (A), the limitation under paragraph (1) shall be the sum of the limitations under paragraph (1) to which each spouse would be entitled if such spouses had not been married. For purposes of the preceding sentence, each spouse shall be treated as owning the property during the period that either spouse owned the property.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(b)(2)(B) (src:25-26)
GIVEN `a husband and wife make a joint return for the taxable year of the sale or exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (2)(A) is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the first spouse's limitation if not married` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the second spouse's limitation if not married` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 121(b)(2)(B) the limitation for other joint returns` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`a husband and wife make a joint return for the taxable year of the sale or exchange`) THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a husband and wife who make a joint return"
            NOTHING
        IF `paragraph (2)(A) is met` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN
            CONSIDER `the first spouse's limitation if not married`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST first THEN
                CONSIDER `the second spouse's limitation if not married`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                WHEN JUST second THEN JUST (first PLUS second)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If such spouses do not meet the requirements of subparagraph (A)" -- when they do meet (A), or whether they do is not covered, this subparagraph does not set the limitation.
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `Subsection (b)(3): application to only 1 sale or exchange every 2 years`

-- src:27 | (3) Application to only 1 sale or exchange every 2 years
-- src:28 | Subsection (a) shall not apply to any sale or exchange by the taxpayer if, during the 2-year period ending on the date of such sale or exchange, there was any other sale or exchange by the taxpayer to which subsection (a) applied.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(b)(3) (src:27-28)
GIVEN sale IS A DATE
      `the dates of other sales or exchanges by the taxpayer to which subsection (a) applied` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(b)(3) subsection (a) shall not apply because of another sale or exchange within 2 years` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN d YIELD `the date is in the span` d (`the span of the years ending on` sale 2)) `the dates of other sales or exchanges by the taxpayer to which subsection (a) applied`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (a) shall not apply to any sale or exchange by the taxpayer if, during the 2-year period ending on the date of such sale or exchange, there was any other sale or exchange by the taxpayer to which subsection (a) applied." (the "if" failed: no other such sale within the 2 years; marginal reading (a))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§ `Subsection (b)(4): special rule for certain sales by surviving spouses`

-- src:29 | (4) Special rule for certain sales by surviving spouses
-- src:30 | In the case of a sale or exchange of property by an unmarried individual whose spouse is deceased on the date of such sale, paragraph (1) shall be applied by substituting “$500,000” for “$250,000” if such sale occurs not later than 2 years after the date of death of such spouse and the requirements of paragraph (2)(A) were met immediately before such date of death.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(b)(4) (src:29-30)
GIVEN `an unmarried individual whose spouse is deceased on the date of the sale` IS A BOOLEAN
      sale IS A DATE
      `the date of death of the spouse` IS A DATE
      `the requirements of paragraph (2)(A) were met immediately before the date of death` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(b)(4) paragraph (1) is applied by substituting $500,000 for $250,000` MEANS
    IF `an unmarried individual whose spouse is deceased on the date of the sale`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "paragraph (1) shall be applied by substituting “$500,000” for “$250,000” if such sale occurs not later than 2 years after the date of death of such spouse and the requirements of paragraph (2)(A) were met immediately before such date of death" (a failed "if"; marginal reading (a))
    THEN `both are true` (JUST (`the day number of` sale AT MOST `the day number of` (`the date years after` `the date of death of the spouse` 2))) `the requirements of paragraph (2)(A) were met immediately before the date of death`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a sale or exchange of property by an unmarried individual whose spouse is deceased on the date of such sale"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The requirements of paragraph (2)(A) "immediately before" the date of death, read as: at the end of the day before it, on the facts of the two spouses.
-- (b)(2)(A)(i)-(iii) are the requirements; the joint return of the chapeau is not one of them (fork F14).
-- src:30 | In the case of a sale or exchange of property by an unmarried individual whose spouse is deceased on the date of such sale, paragraph (1) shall be applied by substituting “$500,000” for “$250,000” if such sale occurs not later than 2 years after the date of death of such spouse and the requirements of paragraph (2)(A) were met immediately before such date of death.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(b)(4), paragraph (2)(A) immediately before death (src:30)
GIVEN `the survivor's holding` IS A Holding
      `the deceased spouse's holding` IS A Holding
      `the date of death of the spouse` IS A DATE
      `the dates of other sales or exchanges by the survivor to which subsection (a) applied` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the dates of other sales or exchanges by the deceased spouse to which subsection (a) applied` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(b)(4) the requirements of paragraph (2)(A) were met immediately before the date of death` MEANS
    `both are true`
        (`s 121(b)(2)(A)(i) either spouse meets the ownership requirements of subsection (a)`
            (`s 121(a) the ownership requirement is met` (survivor's `periods of ownership`) window asAt 0)
            (`s 121(a) the ownership requirement is met` (deceased's `periods of ownership`) window asAt 0))
        (`both are true`
            (`s 121(b)(2)(A)(ii) both spouses meet the use requirements of subsection (a)`
                (`s 121(a) the use requirement is met` (survivor's `periods of use as the principal residence`) window asAt 0)
                (`s 121(a) the use requirement is met` (deceased's `periods of use as the principal residence`) window asAt 0))
            (`s 121(b)(2)(A)(iii) neither spouse is ineligible by reason of paragraph (3)`
                (`s 121(b)(3) subsection (a) shall not apply because of another sale or exchange within 2 years` asAt `the dates of other sales or exchanges by the survivor to which subsection (a) applied`)
                (`s 121(b)(3) subsection (a) shall not apply because of another sale or exchange within 2 years` asAt `the dates of other sales or exchanges by the deceased spouse to which subsection (a) applied`)))
    WHERE
        survivor MEANS `the survivor's holding`
        deceased MEANS `the deceased spouse's holding`
        asAt MEANS `the date with day number` (`the day number of` `the date of death of the spouse` MINUS 1)
        window MEANS `s 121(a) the 5-year period ending on the date of the sale or exchange` asAt

§ `Subsection (b)(5): exclusion of gain allocated to nonqualified use`

-- (D): the order. (A) works on the gain left after (d)(6); (B) is applied without regard to the gain to which (d)(6) applies.
-- src:49 | (i) subparagraph (A) shall be applied after the application of subsection (d)(6), and
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(b)(5)(D)(i) (src:49)
GIVEN gain IS A NUMBER
      `the gain to which subsection (d)(6) applies` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 121(b)(5)(D)(i) the gain to which subparagraph (A) is applied after the application of subsection (d)(6)` MEANS
    gain MINUS `the gain to which subsection (d)(6) applies`

-- src:50 | (ii) subparagraph (B) shall be applied without regard to any gain to which subsection (d)(6) applies.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(b)(5)(D)(ii) (src:50)
GIVEN gain IS A NUMBER
      `the gain to which subsection (d)(6) applies` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 121(b)(5)(D)(ii) the gain to which subparagraph (B) is applied, without regard to the gain to which (d)(6) applies` MEANS
    `s 121(b)(5)(D)(i) the gain to which subparagraph (A) is applied after the application of subsection (d)(6)` gain `the gain to which subsection (d)(6) applies`

-- (C)(i): any period (other than the portion before January 1, 2009) during which the property is not used as the principal residence of the taxpayer or the taxpayer's spouse or former spouse.
-- (C)(ii): three exceptions: (I) the part of the 5-year period after the last use by the taxpayer or spouse; (II) qualified official extended duty, up to 10 years in all;
-- (III) other temporary absence, up to 2 years in all, for change of employment, health conditions, or unforeseen circumstances the Secretary specifies.
-- The caps are counted in days, as the days in 10 and in 2 years ending on the date of the sale (fork F6, F10).
-- src:41 | The term “period of nonqualified use” means any period (other than the portion of any period preceding January 1, 2009) during which the property is not used as the principal residence of the taxpayer or the taxpayer’s spouse or former spouse.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(b)(5)(C)(i) (src:41)
GIVEN `periods of ownership` IS A LIST OF Span
      `periods used as the principal residence of the taxpayer or the taxpayer's spouse or former spouse` IS A LIST OF Span
GIVETH A LIST OF Span
`s 121(b)(5)(C)(i) the periods of nonqualified use` MEANS
    `the spans less the spans` (`the spans from` (`the spans with no day counted twice` `periods of ownership`) (Date 1 1 2009)) `periods used as the principal residence of the taxpayer or the taxpayer's spouse or former spouse`

-- src:44 | (I) any portion of the 5-year period described in subsection (a) which is after the last date that such property is used as the principal residence of the taxpayer or the taxpayer’s spouse,
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(b)(5)(C)(ii)(I) (src:44)
GIVEN `periods used as the principal residence of the taxpayer or the taxpayer's spouse` IS A LIST OF Span
      window IS A Span
GIVETH A LIST OF Span
`s 121(b)(5)(C)(ii)(I) the portion of the 5-year period after the last date the property is used as the principal residence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the latest last day of the spans` `periods used as the principal residence of the taxpayer or the taxpayer's spouse`
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): with no use as the principal residence there is no "last date" for a portion to be after.
    WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
    WHEN JUST lastUse THEN LIST (`the overlap of the spans` window (Span OF (`the date with day number` (`the day number of` lastUse PLUS 1)), window's `last day`))

-- src:45 | (II) any period (not to exceed an aggregate period of 10 years) during which the taxpayer or the taxpayer’s spouse is serving on qualified official extended duty (as defined in subsection (d)(9)(C)) described in clause (i), (ii), or (iii) of subsection (d)(9)(A), and
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(b)(5)(C)(ii)(II) (src:45)
GIVEN nonqualified IS A LIST OF Span
      `the periods of qualified official extended duty described in clause (i), (ii) or (iii) of subsection (d)(9)(A)` IS A LIST OF Span
      sale IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 121(b)(5)(C)(ii)(II) the days of qualified official extended duty, not to exceed an aggregate of 10 years` MEANS
    `the smaller of`
        (`the days in both lists inside the window` nonqualified (`the spans with no day counted twice` `the periods of qualified official extended duty described in clause (i), (ii) or (iii) of subsection (d)(9)(A)`) (Span OF (Date 1 1 1900), (Date 31 12 9999)))
        (`the days in the years ending on` sale 10)

-- src:46 | (III) any other period of temporary absence (not to exceed an aggregate period of 2 years) due to change of employment, health conditions, or such other unforeseen circumstances as may be specified by the Secretary.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(b)(5)(C)(ii)(III) (src:46)
GIVEN nonqualified IS A LIST OF Span
      absences IS A LIST OF `Temporary absence`
      sale IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 121(b)(5)(C)(ii)(III) the days of other temporary absence, not to exceed an aggregate of 2 years` MEANS
    `the smaller of`
        (`the days in both lists inside the window` nonqualified (`the spans with no day counted twice` qualifyingAbsences) (Span OF (Date 1 1 1900), (Date 31 12 9999)))
        (`the days in the years ending on` sale 2)
    WHERE
        qualifyingAbsences MEANS
            map (GIVEN a YIELD a's `days`)
                (filter (GIVEN a YIELD    a's `change of employment`
                                       OR a's `health conditions`
                                       OR a's `unforeseen circumstances as may be specified by the Secretary`) absences)

-- src:38 | (C) Period of nonqualified use
-- src:39 | For purposes of this paragraph—
-- src:40 | (i) In general
-- src:41 | The term “period of nonqualified use” means any period (other than the portion of any period preceding January 1, 2009) during which the property is not used as the principal residence of the taxpayer or the taxpayer’s spouse or former spouse.
-- src:42 | (ii) Exceptions
-- src:43 | The term “period of nonqualified use” does not include—
-- src:44 | (I) any portion of the 5-year period described in subsection (a) which is after the last date that such property is used as the principal residence of the taxpayer or the taxpayer’s spouse,
-- src:45 | (II) any period (not to exceed an aggregate period of 10 years) during which the taxpayer or the taxpayer’s spouse is serving on qualified official extended duty (as defined in subsection (d)(9)(C)) described in clause (i), (ii), or (iii) of subsection (d)(9)(A), and
-- src:46 | (III) any other period of temporary absence (not to exceed an aggregate period of 2 years) due to change of employment, health conditions, or such other unforeseen circumstances as may be specified by the Secretary.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(b)(5)(C) (src:38-46)
GIVEN `periods of ownership` IS A LIST OF Span
      `periods used as the principal residence of the taxpayer or the taxpayer's spouse or former spouse` IS A LIST OF Span
      `periods used as the principal residence of the taxpayer or the taxpayer's spouse` IS A LIST OF Span
      window IS A Span
      sale IS A DATE
      `the periods of qualified official extended duty described in clause (i), (ii) or (iii) of subsection (d)(9)(A)` IS A LIST OF Span
      absences IS A LIST OF `Temporary absence`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 121(b)(5)(C) the aggregate days of nonqualified use` MEANS
    daysAfterExceptionI MINUS exceptionII MINUS exceptionIII
    WHERE
        afterExceptionI MEANS
            `the spans less the spans`
                (`s 121(b)(5)(C)(i) the periods of nonqualified use` `periods of ownership` `periods used as the principal residence of the taxpayer or the taxpayer's spouse or former spouse`)
                (`s 121(b)(5)(C)(ii)(I) the portion of the 5-year period after the last date the property is used as the principal residence` `periods used as the principal residence of the taxpayer or the taxpayer's spouse` window)
        daysAfterExceptionI MEANS `the days in the spans of a list` afterExceptionI
        exceptionII MEANS `s 121(b)(5)(C)(ii)(II) the days of qualified official extended duty, not to exceed an aggregate of 10 years` afterExceptionI `the periods of qualified official extended duty described in clause (i), (ii) or (iii) of subsection (d)(9)(A)` sale
        exceptionIII MEANS `s 121(b)(5)(C)(ii)(III) the days of other temporary absence, not to exceed an aggregate of 2 years` (`the spans less the spans` afterExceptionI `the periods of qualified official extended duty described in clause (i), (ii) or (iii) of subsection (d)(9)(A)`) absences sale

-- (B): the ratio of the aggregate periods of nonqualified use to the period the property was owned.
-- src:34 | (B) Gain allocated to periods of nonqualified use
-- src:35 | For purposes of subparagraph (A), gain shall be allocated to periods of nonqualified use based on the ratio which—
-- src:36 | (i) the aggregate periods of nonqualified use during the period such property was owned by the taxpayer, bears to
-- src:37 | (ii) the period such property was owned by the taxpayer.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(b)(5)(B) (src:34-37)
GIVEN `the aggregate days of nonqualified use during the period the property was owned by the taxpayer` IS A NUMBER
      `the days the property was owned by the taxpayer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 121(b)(5)(B) the ratio of the aggregate periods of nonqualified use to the period owned` MEANS
    IF `the days the property was owned by the taxpayer` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN JUST (`the aggregate days of nonqualified use during the period the property was owned by the taxpayer` DIVIDED BY `the days the property was owned by the taxpayer`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): a ratio to a period of no days is not defined.
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (A): subsection (a) shall not apply to so much of the gain as is allocated to periods of nonqualified use.
-- src:32 | (A) In general
-- src:33 | Subsection (a) shall not apply to so much of the gain from the sale or exchange of property as is allocated to periods of nonqualified use.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(b)(5)(A) (src:32-33)
GIVEN gain IS A NUMBER
      ratio IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 121(b)(5)(A) the gain to which subsection (a) shall not apply, being the gain allocated to periods of nonqualified use` MEANS
    CONSIDER ratio
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): no ratio, no allocation.
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST r THEN JUST (gain TIMES r)
